#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161668 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162102 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac80eed8-d801-5275-9bd1-73ba43fadb38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "162ebeba-e9ee-5588-8d79-659754a77548" :question/math-academy-id "e-10044" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find the marginal mass function for $X.$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.3}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.7}$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, the marginal mass function for $X$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161871 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162071 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "da693f0e-db20-5a7f-9737-3f26d5d6581c" :question/math-academy-id "e-9189" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find $P(X = 0).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{12}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{12}$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\dfrac{7}{12}}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{5}{12}$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $\\dfrac{5}{12}$ | $\\dfrac{7}{12}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0) & ={f}_{X}(0) \\\\  & =f(0,0)+f(0,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161872 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162072 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cumulative Probability Given a Joint Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "e99dc081-a5d6-5770-a0ea-da172b0d37f5" :question/math-academy-id "e-9190" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(X \\geq 2).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f_X(x)$ and $f_Y(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $f_X$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.25}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.5}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}0.25}$ |\n| $f_Y$ | $0.35$ | $0.65$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $X$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ | $0.25$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & =P(X\\in \\{2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =0.5+0.25 \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162072 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cumulative Probability Given a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bd57af1-7d1c-5a33-86ee-75a99adf862f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159057} {:answer/id #uuid "c4949a14-dd68-5870-8eac-ee6f1946e222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159058} {:answer/id #uuid "083e837b-2ec9-5df2-ba3d-d1f0563aad88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159059} {:answer/id #uuid "272dc244-3662-559a-9f8a-dbaebde63ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159060} {:answer/id #uuid "599a2b1b-7775-57a1-bb2d-ec733f0c182b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "083e837b-2ec9-5df2-ba3d-d1f0563aad88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159059} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3c90ebe-b224-55df-b9c4-1fdf615053da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "040f74e5-7507-505e-befe-d132e8cdef58" :question/math-academy-id "q-110400" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(Y\\le 2).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ | $0.6$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.3$ | $0.35$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $Y$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $0.35$ | $0.35$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\le 2) & =P(Y\\in \\{1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(Y=1)+P(Y=2) \\\\  & =0.3+0.35 \\\\  & =0.65.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162071 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e6364f8-ede1-568c-9447-7d8512d55750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269839} {:answer/id #uuid "89a2d1f9-b60b-5ec4-add3-d4cba31eb01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270457} {:answer/id #uuid "a59e14ce-d806-5a21-85ba-749c56d7d474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270752} {:answer/id #uuid "b4316442-e48c-5a9f-970b-60c4e4e62eff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270874} {:answer/id #uuid "d8176f53-7cdf-5ca4-a8a3-04aab032e066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a59e14ce-d806-5a21-85ba-749c56d7d474" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270752} :answer-field/id #uuid "677b355b-9aaf-545c-9e9f-5ddacac81e3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81d1721a-cc20-5d10-aa30-7f257189469f" :question/math-academy-id "q-142557" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find ${f}_{Y}(2).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.35$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(2) & =f(0,2)+f(1,2) \\\\  & =0.2+0.05 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425145 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162071 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96760d15-5e56-529b-a5da-1697dc782031" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2da33fc0-18c6-5b5b-9178-dc0d38d868b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425127} {:answer/id #uuid "2e02ef30-7705-5bf7-ae13-d466e60d3409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425128} {:answer/id #uuid "49227992-7dad-5c8e-8853-4765f7f38dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425130} {:answer/id #uuid "75066fec-23f7-5ab3-a28a-b3a3c440ffe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425133} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f5f9e3-2ce5-5e18-b115-a3bc9bec3641" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e02ef30-7705-5bf7-ae13-d466e60d3409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425128} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9f24a0a-a03d-56b3-b962-7005c236dd29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425143}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7843f1c8-1167-5bc2-84a4-7db8f3081808" :question/math-academy-id "q-142567" :question/problem "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find ${f}_{X}(3).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.35$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.35$ | $0.3$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(3) & =f(3,0)+f(3,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.2+0.1+0.05 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162072 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Cumulative Probability Given a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b199b00-2e32-51b7-a0a2-2af7edc30793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269945} {:answer/id #uuid "a48bdf26-5f1a-5acc-91d7-652daba55fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270736} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7ab526-7b74-5841-a507-644509a22dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270792} {:answer/id #uuid "e233ef36-ef94-5e6c-895a-e363b992f2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271256} {:answer/id #uuid "e984de61-29d8-5c1f-b4c2-570abff33fd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e233ef36-ef94-5e6c-895a-e363b992f2f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271256} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c1240f6-22a0-5c0f-bdb8-d662a62e2820" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d18fe4f-c908-58f7-9a78-04f4bc6d6db6" :question/math-academy-id "q-142718" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(|Y|>0).$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=-1$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.55$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $Y$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.35$ | $0.45$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(|Y|>0) & =P(Y\\in \\{-1,1\\}) \\\\  & =P(Y=-1)+P(Y=1) \\\\  & =0.2+0.45 \\\\  & =0.65.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425146 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162102 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac80eed8-d801-5275-9bd1-73ba43fadb38" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Mar