\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find the marginal mass function for $Y.$" :question/worked-solution "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, the marginal mass function for $Y$ is given by the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ |"}]}
